# **Build-side rules only.** This repository is `handler/` and the workflow that builds it;
# nothing here generates a tree, so this file is short and that is the correct length rather
# than a sign something was dropped in the migration. Test fixtures, measurement records and
# history bundles have rules of their own, in the repository that holds those trees.

.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# **Credentials, and this repository is public.** Neither is read at build time — the workflow
# takes its secrets from Actions and the worker takes its own from the job envelope — so a file
# by either name here is a local convenience that must never become a commit. Ignored by name
# so that `git add -A` cannot publish one irreversibly.
.env
.venv/
